## Architecture: Domain-Centric Architecture (DCA)

This project follows DCA. The architecture rules run with `{{verifyCommand}}`; every change — by hand or in a
delivery pipeline — keeps them green.

- conventions: `{{conventionsPath}}` — layout, suffixes, allowed imports, the resolved framework configuration

Before constructing anything (aggregate, use case, adapter, event, context), look it up in the DCA knowledge
catalog through `dca-knowledge` and build from the recipe and template it names. Never invent a DCA convention
from memory; where the catalog does not cover it, say so.

The skill that carries each kind of work — use it in a session as a delivery stage does:

{{#if build}}
- build: `dca-modelling` — tactical domain types: aggregates, entities, value objects, events, domain services, failures
{{/if}}
{{#if guard}}
- guard: `dca-discipline` — the invariants while editing domain, application and adapter code
{{/if}}
{{#if glossary}}
- glossary: `ubiquitous-language` — a new domain term enters its context's glossary before it appears in code
{{/if}}
{{#if map}}
- map: `context-map` — the designed context map, when a context or a relationship between contexts changes
{{/if}}
{{#if browserTests}}
- browser tests: `e2e-testing` — end-user tests through the browser
{{/if}}
{{#if review}}
- review: {{reviewSkills}} — before a change is committed
{{/if}}
<!-- dca-core: end -->
